blankpages@gmail.com (essej) wrote:
>we're trying to find (or compose, i suppose) a definitive list of
>character class differences and abilities because we have some
>questions we can't find the answers to.
>
>for example, are any classes blocked from casting certain classes of
>magic?

No, but some spells aren't really very useful until you're at Skilled or
better in their school of magic (others, it doesn't really matter).

>do any classes have spellcasting benefits?

All classes have one spell they are unusually good at casting,
appropriate to their role.

>are any classes
>prohibited from using certain weapon types?

No.  However, using weapons in which you are restricted is usually not a
very good idea unless they're much better than any non-restricted weapon
you've got available.

>if you're a priest(ess),
>does wisdom act as your spellcasting success/hunger adjusting
>attribute?

Only wizards get a reduced/zero food cost for having a high value in
their spellcasting attribute.

Knights, priests, monks, healers, and valkyries use wisdom to cast
spells; everyone else uses intelligence.
